xv6 is a re-implementation of Dennis Ritchie's and Ken Thompson's Unix
Version 6 (v6).  xv6 loosely follows the structure and style of v6,
but is implemented for a 32-bit MIPS (mipsel) uniprocessor, targeting
QEMU's "malta" machine, using ANSI C.

ACKNOWLEDGMENTS

See README.common at the top of this repository for the acknowledgments
shared by every port here - John Lions's Commentary, the contributor
list, and the copyright.  What follows is specific to this port.

BUILDING AND RUNNING XV6

From the repository root: run ./configure once (it detects a mipsel
cross toolchain and a qemu-system-mipsel on this machine), then
`make build-mips`, `make run-mips` (interactive shell under QEMU), or
`make test-mips` (boots headless and runs the usertests suite).
